From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:03:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posture: add host options and per-client posture flags

Plumbing that the later patches read:

- config: touch_posture_diagonal_mm (default 356, strict 100..419 parse with a
  warning and fallback), touch_tablet_mode (default on) and handheld_mode
  (tablet | xbox_fullscreen | desktop, default xbox_fullscreen);
- paired client record: touch_device (a stock client that cannot send a posture
  can be flagged) and posture_mode (auto, desktop, tablet, handheld), persisted
  in sunshine_state.json only when not default, listed by /api/clients/list and
  settable through /api/clients/update with validation;
- launch session: carries the validated posture hints (client_posture), copied
  into the RTSP snapshot.

The options have no effect until the policy is wired into launch and resume.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
